{"k":"note","text":"FIXTURE (SYNTHETIC, SCHEMA-UNFROZEN): the RICH twin of scene-abs-loop.asmtrace. Its header, codeimage and 13 trace events are copied verbatim from that generated golden; the four `mem` events below are HAND-AUTHORED and measure nothing. `mem` is a RESERVED registry row in docs/internal/gui/asmtrace-schema.md with NO v1 producer, so no recorder can emit this file — the {step,ea,size,rw} shape is the one 10-spacetime-3d-overview.md PROPOSES and it is NOT FROZEN. When the Wave-1 memory stream lands, replace this file with a recorded one rather than freezing the schema around it."}
{"k":"note","text":"every `ea` here lies at 0x200000, outside every `codeimage` region. Before 54 T1 this was INERT-BUT-PRESENT under the coarse-rung projection (regions_from_codeimage alone): these accesses mapped to no region and the terrain gained no data cell. 54 T1 (2026-08-02) closed that gap in the real shipping path (ui/shell.cpp) by appending space::observed_data_spans — an Unknown-kind 'observed data' span clustered from exactly these addresses — to the region set before build_projection, so the rich rung now lights there too. test_scene_fbo.cpp's build_scene() test helper deliberately calls build_projection directly, without that extension, to keep pinning the coarse-only primitive contract this note originally described; desktop/test/test_drillin.cpp exercises the explicit-data-region opt-in (as 07's /proc/pid/maps snapshot will supply), and test_terrain.cpp's Fixture O exercises the observed-span path end to end."}
